                    "fact": {"id": "heyho-pammelia", "text": {"en": "This round was printed in 1609 in Pammelia, the earliest printed English book of rounds and catches, credited to Thomas Ravenscroft. There it is a round for five voices.", "es": "Este canon se imprimió en 1609 en Pammelia, el libro inglés de cánones y catches impreso más antiguo, atribuido a Thomas Ravenscroft. Allí es un canon a cinco voces."}, "source": {"en": "[Thomas Ravenscroft, compiler], Pammelia (London: William Barley, 1609), p. 41, No. 85, read from the facsimile (the 1971 Da Capo Press reprint, also on IMSLP); and William H. Husk, \"Pammelia\", in George Grove, ed., A Dictionary of Music and Musicians, vol. 2 (London: Macmillan, 1880), p. 643", "es": "[Thomas Ravenscroft, compilador], Pammelia (Londres: William Barley, 1609), p. 41, n.º 85, leído en el facsímil (la reimpresión de Da Capo Press de 1971, también en IMSLP); y William H. Husk, \"Pammelia\", en George Grove, ed., A Dictionary of Music and Musicians, vol. 2 (Londres: Macmillan, 1880), p. 643"}, "url": "https://imslp.org/wiki/Pammelia_(Ravenscroft,_Thomas)"}
